line-height: 150%;"><em><span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 150%;"><br>Robert Levin</span></em></span></p></td> </tr> </tbody></table> <!-- End Paragraph 1 --> </td> </tr>   <tr> <td align="left" valign="top"> <!-- Start Paragraph 2 --> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"> <tbody><tr> <td dir="ltr" align="left" valign="top" style="padding: 0px 20px 0px 20px" class="match pad20rl wrap"><p style="font-size: 14px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 150%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #757575; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="col1_p2_text" data-groupid="col1_p2" class="mobile_match"><br data-mce-bogus="1"></p></td> </tr> </tbody></table> <!-- End Paragraph 2 --> </td> </tr>    <tr> <td align="left" valign="top"> <!-- Start Footnote --> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"> <tbody><tr> <td dir="ltr" align="left" valign="top" style="padding: 0px 20px 10px 20px;" class="match pad20rl wrap"><p style="font-size: 14px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 150%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #000000; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="col1_p3_text" data-groupid="col1_p3" class="mobile_match"></p></td> </tr> </tbody></table> <!-- End Footnote --> </td> </tr>  </tbody></table> </th> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 2-005: 50% Image | 50% Text + CTA --> </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td><table role="presentation" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="640" border="0" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="wrap"><tbody><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-008: Paragraph | P1 --><section id="1008_p1" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td valign="top" align="left"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="wrap"> <tbody><tr> <td align="left" style="padding: 0px 20px 16px 20px" class="pad20rl match"><p style="font-size: 14px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 150%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #333333; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="p1_text" data-groupid="p1" class="mobile_match"><span style="font-size: 16px; color: #333333; line-height: 150%;">Cowriting the second edition of <a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/featured-insights/mckinsey-on-books/rewired?__hScId__=v710000019e8eae06799e6debf4bbe5c898&__hRlId__=4ae28ed3b10547860000021ef3a0bccf&__hDId__=4ae28ed3-b105-4786-93d0-d92489cb053e&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-nsl-mkq-mgp-glb--&hlkid=a95f66821273425e91cd26b1eab74a33&hctky=17208988&hdpid=4ae28ed3-b105-4786-93d0-d92489cb053e" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: none;" data-link-id="7e25d3305eac11f18c10d59c2914dbbe"><span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><em>Rewired: How Leading Companies Win with Technology and AI</em></span></a> (Wiley, April 2026) was a strange experience.<br><br>The technology landscape had changed so much since the first edition. In just a few years, we moved from machine learning models that generated insights for humans to act on to generative AI copilots and now to early agentic systems that can operate autonomously across entire workflows. The acceleration has been radical and the opportunities unprecedented. We are living through a generational moment.<br><br>Amid all the change and growing pains, however, the central lesson of the book’s first edition still holds: Turning technology into value depends on building the organizational capabilities to properly harness the tech. We call it the “how engine.” The technology may evolve (from digital to AI to quantum) but the need for a high-performing “how engine” does not.<br><br>The importance of this “how” is particularly germane now with AI value realization only just beginning to scale. The latest data from McKinsey’s <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/capabilities/quantumblack/our-insights/the-state-of-ai?__hScId__=v710000019e8eae06799e6debf4bbe5c898&__hRlId__=4ae28ed3b10547860000021ef3a0bcd0&__hDId__=4ae28ed3-b105-4786-93d0-d92489cb053e&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-nsl-mkq-mgp-glb--&hlkid=30f7b3ff9297458494d90f5341390491&hctky=17208988&hdpid=4ae28ed3-b105-4786-93d0-d92489cb053e" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="952b88405eac11f18c10d59c2914dbbe">State of AI</a></span> report shows that nearly nine in ten organizations are already using AI in at least one function, and many are experimenting with agentic systems. But most companies have not yet begun <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/capabilities/mckinsey-technology/our-insights/building-the-foundations-for-agentic-ai-at-scale?__hScId__=v710000019e8eae06799e6debf4bbe5c898&__hRlId__=4ae28ed3b10547860000021ef3a0bcd1&__hDId__=4ae28ed3-b105-4786-93d0-d92489cb053e&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-nsl-mkq-mgp-glb--&hlkid=0922411917fe4119980ae4e0799e6f6e&hctky=17208988&hdpid=4ae28ed3-b105-4786-93d0-d92489cb053e" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="a2c129b05eac11f18c10d59c2914dbbe">scaling these capabilities enterprise-wide</a></span>, and even fewer have deployed agentic AI meaningfully even within a single function.&nbsp;<br><br>That gap between technological potential and organizational readiness is what we think of as the <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/capabilities/quantumblack/our-insights/seizing-the-agentic-ai-advantage?__hScId__=v710000019e8eae06799e6debf4bbe5c898&__hRlId__=4ae28ed3b10547860000021ef3a0bcd2&__hDId__=4ae28ed3-b105-4786-93d0-d92489cb053e&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-nsl-mkq-mgp-glb--&hlkid=2067b397ca744bd7ad228215db8bbb1c&hctky=17208988&hdpid=4ae28ed3-b105-4786-93d0-d92489cb053e" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="af6ae4805eac11f18c10d59c2914dbbe">AI value paradox</a></span>: The capability of AI has outpaced companies’ ability to reorganize around it. That’s not unusual. Every major technology wave has exhibited this dynamic. What’s different this time is the pace.<br><br>Many of the companies that have been keeping up and thriving as this phase unfolds are the ones that have built strong foundational capabilities. The companies featured in the book’s first edition—Freeport and DBS—were succeeding then and are succeeding now. Not because they picked the right model or vendor, but because they built the capabilities to identify value, redesign work, reskill talent, and scale change across the enterprise while investing in enabling technology and data stack modernization. (This is also true of the other 20 leading companies we analyzed for the book.)<br></span></p></td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-008: Paragraph | P1 --> </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td><table role="presentation" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="640" border="0" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="wrap"><tbody><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-001: Divider -->
